### Demographic inequities in tree canopy access {#sec-res-demographic}

Block groups were organized into one of four tree canopy access categories based on their PTCC and PTAS values (@tbl-canopy-access). The spatial distribution of each category is illustrated in @fig-canopy-access-map. The least common category is HH, or neighborhoods with both abundant private tree canopy and higher than average access to park tree canopy. These block groups are mostly confined to isolated pockets in the northeastern part of Phoenix. Block groups in the HL category have lower than average access to park trees, but the private tree canopy is abundant. The most common category is LH, representing block groups with low private tree canopy but high access to park canopy cover. These are low-canopy neighborhoods where public parks provide a tree canopy refuge to the residents. They are located mostly in the center and northern portions of the city where most of the public parks are situated. The remaining block groups belong to the LL category, or "tree canopy deserts," lacking both private tree canopy cover and access to public park tree canopy. They tend to be found on the periphery of the city.


::: {#tbl-canopy-access .cell tbl-cap='Tree canopy access categories'}

```{.r .cell-code .hidden}
# Build data frame
canopy_access <- data.frame(
  category = c("HH", "HL", "LH", "LL"),
  rule = c("High PTCC + High PTAS", 
           "High PTCC + Low PTAS", 
           "Low PTCC + High PTAS",
           "Low PTCC + Low PTAS"),
  desc = c("Abundant private and park tree canopy",
           "Self-sufficient private tree canopy",
           "Park tree canopy refuge",
           "Tree canopy desert"),
  bg_pct = c("89 (9.0)", "122 (12.3)", "404 (40.9)", "373 (37.8)")
)

# Create gt table
canopy_access |> 
  gt() |> 
  cols_label(
    category = "Category",
    rule = "Rule",
    desc = "Description",
    bg_pct = md("*n* Block groups (%)"),
  ) |> 
  tab_footnote(footnote = md(paste0("*N* = 988 total block groups"))) |> 
  tab_style(
    style = cell_text(align = "left"),
    locations = list(cells_footnotes())
  )
```

